{"kind":"check","severity":"error","code":"E0519","message":"the scope arguments of the annotated contract for projection `Scope.pathInValue` (requiredUpperBound) do not cover the scope selected by the local Scope rule (knownUpperBound) (unknownSource)","primary":{"file":"<wt>/docs/2026-10-27-TODO-142_256_283_287-permission-and-effect-mechanisms/r40.3/inputs/unknown-source.bnt","start":{"line":3,"column":28,"offset":119},"end":{"line":3,"column":45,"offset":136},"label":"`Scope.pathInValue` is not covered by `the annotated scope contract (requiredUpperBound)`"},"secondary":[],"notes":["the scope arguments of the annotated contract (requiredUpperBound) must cover the scope selected by the local Scope rule for this call (knownUpperBound); for widening, the destination must also cover the source contract","reason: unknownSource","requiredUpperBound: [\"/data/a\"]","knownUpperBound: Top (all targets)","source: no local provenance for the same successful checked value at this call","scope call: .sample at surface preorder 0"],"helps":[{"message":"If the call is nested in an expression, move it to the right-hand side of `bind` and use that name. If the value is a parameter or handler clause parameter with only a narrow type annotation, `bind` alone does not establish provenance. To keep the narrow contract, do not project or widen it here: pass it unchanged to a scoped entry that accepts the same narrow type, such as `File.readTextIn`, or widen it in the caller where the checked value is bound and declare the parameter with the wider type. To accept all targets instead, remove the parameter's scope arguments; callers must then widen to the unscoped type with `Scope.widenPathIn` or `Http.widenRequestIn`. Widening a Top input also requires a result without scope arguments. For a handler clause parameter, using Top also requires the protected body to select Top and may require a broader `uses` annotation.","edits":[]}]}
